“When do you use Python?”

Correct answer:

“When I need reproducible analysis, automation, or more complex transformations than Excel or SQL can easily handle.”


A complex transformation is when:

Excel becomes messy or manual

SQL becomes hard to read or maintain

You need logic + repetition + flexibility

Python handles these cleanly.


If asked again, you can say:

“I use Python when analysis requires multi-step transformations, conditional logic, time-based calculations, or reproducible workflows that would be inefficient or error-prone in Excel or SQL.”



SQL → PYTHON MAPPING (IMPORTANT)

What you already know:

Concept	SQL	Python
Filter	WHERE	df[df[...]]
Group	GROUP BY	groupby()
Conditional	CASE WHEN	if / np.where
Aggregation	SUM, AVG	sum(), mean()

This is why Python felt familiar — it’s the same thinking.
